      "patient_response": "Hi, Dr. Smith. Well, I came in because... I've been having this issue with how I'm talking lately. Like at work, I'm a jeweler, and when a customer asks me a really simple question—like when a ring repair will be ready—my answer just goes all over the place. \n\nI'll start out talking about the invoices, and then somehow that turns into talking about garden soil, and then suddenly I'm on about mortgage papers. I can just see them losing me, like they have no idea what I'm saying. It's just getting really hard to communicate clearly, and I need to figure out what's going on.",
